      "source_name": "UN News, 28 August 2026",
      "note": "\"More than 10,000 households along the Trishuli corridor need emergency shelter and relief supplies.\" A count of households in need, not of homes destroyed. One resettled community of 250 households on the low banks of the Trishuli — rebuilt there after the 2015 earthquake — was swept away entirely, per CARE Nepal's country director Mona Sherpa."
    }
